  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["C2"],
      "pins": ["C2.1", "C2.2"],
      "nets": ["Display_Power_Switch", "GND"],
      "observed": "On the EPD_Driver sheet the bulk decoupling capacitor C2 on the Display_Power_Switch node is drawn with the value '1mF/6.3V' (milli-Farad = 1000 µF). Every other capacitor on the board is written with the 'u' prefix (e.g. C1 0.1uF/16V, C4 1uF/25V, C13 10uF), so C2 is the lone 'm' entry.",
      "expected": "The specification's component-matching table requires C2 = 1 µF/6.3 V (the G1-group bulk cap for the Waveshare 2.13\" panel). 1 mF is three orders of magnitude too large.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "C1 (G1 group only): 1 µF/6.3 V | C2 = 1 µF/6.3 V | Matches G1-specific value (EPD_Driver.kicad_sch matching table)"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "C2 1mF/6.3V, connected between Display_Power_Switch and GND (Sheet /EPD_Driver/)"}
      ],
      "impact": "A 1000 µF bulk cap on the GPIO-switched display rail would draw a large inrush current each time Q2 turns the EPD power on, sagging the +3V3 rail and potentially brown-out/resetting the SKW92A, and the value cannot physically fit the small SMD footprint intended for a 1 µF/6.3 V part.",
      "confidence": 0.7
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The schematic otherwise matches the specification (FAN53610 topology, EPD boost/charge-pump parts, Q2 high-side switch, keyboard/SD/Ethernet/UART connectivity), but C2 on the EPD_Driver sheet is drawn as 1 mF/6.3 V instead of the specified 1 µF/6.3 V — a 1000× value error that is the lone 'm' prefix on the board and is treated as an anomaly."
}

